# Routing in apps/web

This app is an MPA (`ssr: true`). Top-level pages are `/gardens` and `/my-garden`. Data fetching details live in the web data-fetching rule.

## Split

| Route | Kind | Data |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/gardens` | SPA island | Client `useQuery` only. No server `loader` for garden/plant data |
| `/my-garden` | MPA | Static stub. No server `loader` |

`/` redirects to `/gardens`. Nested `/gardens/:id` stays client-side later. Do not add more top-level documents without updating this rule.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Keep `ssr: true` in `react-router.config.ts`
- Use `Link` with `reloadDocument` between `/gardens` and `/my-garden`
- Fetch gardens/plants with `useQuery` in the gardens page
- Keep `/my-garden` static until the feature is implemented

**Don't**

- Set `ssr: false`
- Client-navigate between `/gardens` and `/my-garden`
- Prefetch gardens in a server `loader` (`dehydrate` / `HydrationBoundary`)
- Fetch my-garden/user data with `useQuery` or a server `loader`

```tsx
<Link to="/my-garden" reloadDocument>
  My Garden
</Link>
```

```tsx
<Link to="/my-garden">My Garden</Link>
```
